{
    "59739": {
        "order_id": 1,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>A binary operation * is defined on the set of real numbers R, by p*q = p + q - \\(\\frac{pq}{2}\\), where p, q \\(\\in\\) R. Find the:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) inverse of&nbsp;-1 under * given that the identity clement is zero.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) truth set of m*&nbsp;7 = m* 5,</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>p*e = e*p = p</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p + e - \\(\\frac{pe}{2}\\) = p</p>\r\n\r\n<p>e - \\(\\frac{pe}{2}\\) = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>e(\\(1 - \\frac{p}{2}\\)) = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>e = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p*p\\(^{-1}\\) = e</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p - p\\(^{-1}\\) - \\(\\frac{pp^{-1}}{2}\\)&nbsp; = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p\\(^{-1}\\) - \\(\\frac{pp}{2}\\) = -p</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p\\(^{-1}\\) (1 - \\(\\frac{p}{2}\\)) = -p</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p\\(^{-1}\\) = \\(\\frac{-p}{1 - \\frac{p}{2}}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Inverse of -1 \\(\\to\\) p = -1</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p\\(^{-1}\\) = \\(\\frac{-1}{1 - (\\frac{-1}{2})} = \\frac{-1}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{-2}{3}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) m*7 = m + 7 - \\(\\frac{7m}{2}\\), m*5 = m + 5 - \\(\\frac{5m}{2}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>m*7 = m*5, m + 7 - \\(\\frac{7m}{2}\\) = m + 5 - \\(\\frac{5m}{2}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>7 - 5 = -\\(\\frac{5m}{2} + \\frac{7m}{2}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2 = \\(\\frac{2m}{2}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>m = 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 1,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 0,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "59740": {
        "order_id": 2,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) Two functions p and q are defined on the set of real numbers, R, by p : y \\(\\to\\) 2y +3 and q : y -&gt; y - 2. Find QOP</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) How many four digits odd numbers greater than 4000 can be formed from 1,7,3,8,2 if repetition is allowed?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>P(y) = 2y + 3, q(y) = y\\(^2\\) - 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>q \\(\\cap\\) p = qp(y)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= q(2y + 3)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= (2y + 3)\\(^3\\) - 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 4xy\\(^2\\) + 12y + 9 - 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 4y\\(^2\\) + 12y + 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img src=\"https://scontent.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.15752-9/p206x206/240612504_382501676719800_6586622837224703747_n.jpg?_nc_cat=106&amp;ccb=1-5&amp;_nc_sid=aee45a&amp;_nc_eui2=AeHCJdwTF637AL-evjiF_Tx2C5mhjcBgFyYLmaGNwGAXJnZKjSG98j-CigdtsghVRnCDGJccYPcJnDYMlb7nTTwo&amp;_nc_ohc=IgYtjWWxS_wAX9OEPNI&amp;_nc_ad=z-m&amp;_nc_cid=0&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.xx&amp;oh=bd27ac15fa4344ff770116d7b763f0e1&amp;oe=614C1976\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No. of ways = 2 x 5 x 5 x 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 250 ways</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 5,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 1,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "59741": {
        "order_id": 3,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>Evaluate; \\(\\int^3_1(3x - 2)^5 dx\\)</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>\\(\\int^3_1(3x - 2)^5 dx\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let u = 3x - 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{du}{dx}\\) = 3</p>\r\n\r\n<p>dx = \\(\\frac{dy}{3}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\int^3_1(3x - 2)^5 dx\\) =&nbsp;\\(\\int^7_1 \\frac{u^5}{3} du\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{u^{5 + 1}}{3(5 + 1)}|^7_1\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{u^5}{18}|^7_1\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{7^6}{18} = \\frac{1^6}{18}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{7^6 - 1}{18}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{117649}{18}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 6536</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 3,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 2,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "59742": {
        "order_id": 4,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>If \\(\\frac{3x^2 + 3x - 2}{(x - 1)(x + 1)}\\) = P + \\(\\frac{Q}{x - 1} + \\frac{R}{x - 1}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Find the value of Q and R&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>\\(\\frac{3x^2 + 3x - 2}{(x - 1)(x + 1)}\\) = P + \\(\\frac{Q}{x - 1} + \\frac{R}{x - 1}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Long division</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:500px\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(x^2 - 1\\)</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;3</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>&nbsp;3x\\(^2\\) + 3x - 2</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>&nbsp;-(3x\\(^2\\) - 3x)</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\overline{6x - 2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{6x^{-2}}{(x - 1)(x + 1)}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{Q}{x - 1} + \\frac{R}{x + 1}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6x - 2 = Q (x + 1) + R(x - 1)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let x = -1&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6(-1) - 2 = Q(-1 + 1) + R (-1 - 1)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-6 - 2 = -2R</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{-8}{-2} = \\frac{-2R}{-2}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>R = 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p>From 6x - 2 = Q(x - 1) + R(x - 1)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let x = 1</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6(1) - 2 = Q(1 + 1) + R(1 - 1)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6 - 2 = 2Q&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{4}{2} = \\frac{2Q}{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= Q = 2</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 4,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 3,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "59744": {
        "order_id": 5,
