    "59746": {
        "order_id": 6,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) A bag contains 10 red and 8 green identical balls. Two balls are drawn at random from the bag, one after the other, without replacement. Find the probability&nbsp;that one is red and the other is green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) There are 20% defective bulbs in a large box. If 12 bulbs are selected randomly from the box, calculate the probability that between two and five are defective.&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>No. of red = 10, No of green = 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Total = 18</p>\r\n\r\n<p>P(RG) = P(R) x P(G)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{10}{18} \\times \\frac{8}{17} = \\frac{40}{152}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>P(GR) = P(G) x P(R)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{8}{18} \\times \\frac{10}{17} = \\frac{40}{153}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>P(one red and one green)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{40}{153} + \\frac{40}{153} = \\frac{80}{153}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) P = 20% = \\(\\frac{20}{100}\\) = 0.2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>q = 1 - P = 1 - 0.2 = 0.8</p>\r\n\r\n<p>n = 12</p>\r\n\r\n<p>P(2 \\(\\leq x \\leq 5\\)) = P(5) - P(2)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(^{12}C_5(0.5)^5 (0.8)^7 - ^{12}C_2(0.2)^2(0.8)^{10}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 792 x (0.2)\\(^5\\) (0.8)\\(^7\\) - 65(0.2)\\(^2\\)(0.8)\\(^10\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 0.04892 - 0.2791&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 0.2302</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 8,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 2,
        "_page_idx": 0,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "59747": {
        "order_id": 7,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>Forces F\\(_1\\)(10N, 090&deg;) and F\\(_2\\)(20N, 210\\(^o\\)) and (4N,330&deg;) act on a particle, Find, correct to one decimal place, the magnitude of the resultant force.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>F\\(_1\\) = (10N, 090\\(^o\\)), F\\(_2\\) = (20N, 210\\(^o\\))</p>\r\n\r\n<p>F\\(_3\\) = (4N, 33\\(^o\\))</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img src=\"https://scontent.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.15752-9/p206x206/240655664_425603192228106_8384467034316991621_n.jpg?_nc_cat=102&amp;ccb=1-5&amp;_nc_sid=aee45a&amp;_nc_eui2=AeGSZ6nlz0vtDsrSiT4Ixvew_iS3zV_ttkT-JLfNX-22REs-MUyw6v_ng9Og9sOY5TBDfZ6SexqLgV10B7o45cOH&amp;_nc_ohc=i2b65vLK9bwAX9XNFAq&amp;_nc_ad=z-m&amp;_nc_cid=0&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.xx&amp;oh=dbea4a71db4088df2fb8f3342134f5d6&amp;oe=614EC2CF\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>F\\(_3\\) component x - axis&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= - 4 cos 60\\(^o\\)&nbsp; = - 2N</p>\r\n\r\n<p>F\\(_2\\) along y - axis</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 20 x cos 30\\(^o\\) = -1.7320</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img src=\"https://scontent.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.15752-9/p206x206/240639950_272815077654648_4155969325345267960_n.jpg?_nc_cat=105&amp;ccb=1-5&amp;_nc_sid=aee45a&amp;_nc_eui2=AeEn29CVe146PvLTK-NSsLxkWpQ-GdAsMDpalD4Z0CwwOlItqYzTRmKvzvvnIE-wBoVYMRnpGPYS5H63u469OTKp&amp;_nc_ohc=On8nzd5LS2QAX8stRxA&amp;_nc_ad=z-m&amp;_nc_cid=0&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.xx&amp;oh=1cefcd04c7930f130dbf20c08584a700&amp;oe=614DDD9B\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{8N}{-1.732N}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Resultant force</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\sqrt{8^2 + (-1.732)^2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\sqrt{65.999}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 8.185N</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 8.2N</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 3,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 2,
        "_page_idx": 1,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "59748": {
        "order_id": 8,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>Given that w = 8i + 3j, x = 6i - 5j, y = 2i + 3j and |z| = 41. find z in the direction of w + x - 2y.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>W = 8i + 3J</p>\r\n\r\n<p>X = 6i - 5J&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Y = 2i + 3J</p>\r\n\r\n<p>w + x - 2y = 8i + 3j + 6i - 5j - 2(2i + 3j)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 10i - 8j</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Z = \\(\\frac{10i - 8j}{|Z|}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{10i - 8j}{4}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{10i}{4}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{8j}{4}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\)i - 2j</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 2,
        "_page_idx": 2,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "59749": {
        "order_id": 9,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Further Mathematics",
        "topic": null,
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2020",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) If (x&nbsp;+ 2) is a factor of g(x) = 2x\\(^3\\) +11x\\(^2\\) - x - 30, find the zeros of g(x).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Solve 3(2\\(^x\\)) +3\\(^{y - 2}\\) = 25 and 2x -&nbsp;3\\(^{y + 1}\\) = -19 simultaneously.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) Using long division&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:500px\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>&nbsp;x + 2</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>2x\\(^2\\) + 7x - 15</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p>2x\\(^3\\) + 11x^2 - x -30</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>-&nbsp; (2x\\(^3\\) + 4x\\(^2\\))</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\overline{7^2 - x - 30}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>- (7x\\(^2\\) + 14x) - 3</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\overline{-15x - 30}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>- 15x - 30</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p>\\(\\overline{0}\\)</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(x + 2)(2x\\(^2\\) + 7x - 15)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(x + 2)(2x - 3)(x - 5)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>zeros of g (x) are;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x + 2 =0, 2x - 3 = 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x + 5 = 0, x = -2</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x = \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\) and x = -5</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) 3(2^\\(^x\\)) + 3\\(^{y - 2}\\) = 25 .......x1</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2\\(^x\\) - 3\\(^{y + 1}\\) = -19 .........x3</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3(2\\(^x\\)) + 3\\(^{y - 2}\\) = 25</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3\\(^{y - 2}\\)&nbsp;+ 3(3\\(^{y + 1}\\)) = 82</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{3^y}{9} + \\frac{3^y}{1}\\) = 82</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{3^y + 9(3^y)}{9}\\) = 82</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3\\(^y\\) + 9(3\\(^y)\\)) = 82 x 9&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>let p = 3y</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p + qp = 738</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{10p}{10} = \\frac{738}{10}\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>p = 73.8, 3\\(^y\\) = 73.8</p>\r\n\r\n<p>log3\\(^y\\) = log 73.8</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{y log 3}{log 3} = \\frac{log 73.8}{\\log 3}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>y = 3.9</p>\r\n\r\n<p>from&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2\\(^x\\) + 3\\(^{y + 1}\\) = - 19</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2\\(^x\\) + 3\\(^{3.9&nbsp;+ 1}\\) = - 19</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2\\(^x\\) + 3\\(^{4 - 9}\\) = - 19</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2\\(^x\\) -&nbsp;217.7 = - 19</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2\\(^x\\) = 198.71</p>\r\n\r\n<p>log 2\\(^x\\) = log 198.71</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{x \\log 2}{log 2} = \\frac{log 198.71}{log 2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>x&nbsp; = 7.6</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
